A thread that may no longer run stays on the queue it waited on.
A thread unbound while it waited would still take turns;
a thread names a queue only while its account and binding put it on one.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a place names a queue it is not for
Witness: fuzz cores-resume-before-trap

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -343,7 +343,7 @@ static void place_settle(struct place *p)
 #if SCHED_EDF
     core->run_joined |= joined && queue == QUEUE_RUN;
 #endif
-    if (queue != p->queue || core != was) {
+    if (queue != QUEUE_NONE && (queue != p->queue || core != was)) {
         if (p->queue != QUEUE_NONE) {
             place_unqueue(p);
         }
